Lore: The Awakened Core of the Crimson Camp
Within the deep, untamed wilderness of the Land of Dawn’s ancient battlegrounds, the Red Buff has long been known as a primal font of offensive energy, guarded by the ferocious, magma-plated beast known as the Molten Fiend. For centuries, this creature lived as a wordless force of nature, testing the resolve of passing heroes and offering its supreme, damage-enhancing blessing to those strong enough to defeat it in mortal combat. However, as the cataclysmic wars between the Moniyan Empire and the Shadow Abyss began to deeply scar the laylines of the forest, the pure elemental core of the sanctuary was forced to evolve to protect its domain from total corruption. Fusing the raw, burning power of the ancient subterranean rifts with the protective spirit of the forest, the beast transcended its quadrupedal form, awakening as Vulcanus—the sovereign human personification of the Molten Fiend. He now roams the dense jungle canopy as an unyielding sentinel, a wild and independent demi-god who guards the sacred fonts of energy from being abused by corrupt kings or abyssal demons, hunting down any who trespass into his sanctuary with the absolute, terrifying fury of a localized volcanic eruption.

Suggested Atmospheric Background
Vulcanus would look exceptionally magnificent standing upon a cracked granite boulder located deep within a mystical, autumn-themed forest clearing during a dramatic golden sunset. The background should feature towering, gnarled ancient trees with glowing, deep-orange and crimson leaves that sway wildly under a dark, smoke-filled sky filled with sheets of distant, volcanic heat haze. The lighting should be a dramatic, cinematic "Hellfire Flare," where the brilliant, high-contrast neon-yellow light from his eyes and the crystal blade of his glaive cuts sharply through the dark, smoky atmosphere, clashing beautifully with the soft orange and gold glows emanating from his flaming mane. This atmospheric lighting should perfectly illuminate the smooth, dark charcoal-bronze textures of his skin, the sharp spiky layers of his dual-toned mane, and the rich, flowing fabric of his midnight-black trousers. Thick arcs of heat energy and glowing golden particles from his molten aura should be shown grounding into the wet earth around his clawed sabatons, framing his statuesque, predatory silhouette as he stands ready to leap into battle.

The Legendary Profile of Vulcanus
If you've ever played a marksman or a burst assassin in Mobile Legends: Bang Bang, you know the absolute necessity of locking down the "Red Buff" early in the match. To the casual observer tracking the jungle pathways, it appears as an elite, magma-plated monstrosity resting quietly in its pit. But the ancient lore novels and deepest leyline scriptures of the Land of Dawn give this brute his true, terrifying identity: Vulcanus, The Scourge of the Molten Fiend.

