Long before the modern empires began drawing their territorial lines, the prehistoric landscape faced a cataclysmic war involving ancient, forgotten deities. Vulcanus was formed directly from the residual, stubborn consciousness of an ancient Evil God who fell during those primordial battles.

To contain this volatile consciousness from tearing the forest apart, the pure elemental leylines of the jungle bound it into a quadrupedal, magma-plated guardian. However, as the continuous warfare between the Moniyan Empire and the Shadow Abyss deeply scarred the earth, the core evolved. Vulcanus shattered his four-legged prison and awakened as a towering, 196 cm bipedal demi-god. Sporting a volcanic-beast physiology complete with dark stone horns and a voluminous mane of living fire, he stands as the unyielding, independent sentinel of the Crimson Camp.

Why He is Famous (And Brutally Coveted)
Across the competitive history of the realm, Vulcanus is universally celebrated for holding the Soul of Lava—the ultimate damage-enhancing blessing. When a hero survives his trial and conquers him, a portion of his molten essence fractures off, attaching itself to the champion as a floating companion of pure kinetic heat.

This blessing is the exact reason marksmen like Claude, Miya, or Granger become absolute nightmares in the lanes. The Soul of Lava grants their basic attacks a devastating True Damage burning effect that bypasses physical armor entirely, while simultaneously melting the movement speed of their targets. He is famous for the absolute, unrelenting violence of the "30-Second Spawn Marker." The second he materializes in his clearing, every high-tier carry on the map plots a path to his doorstep, knowing that whoever holds the Scourge’s fire controls the tempo of the early game.

The Mythic & Epic Lore Behind His Existence
The scholars of the Magic Academy write that Vulcanus acts as the forest's thermal pressure valve. The deep cracks tracing violently up his charcoal-bronze skin aren't just for show—they are literal tectonic fractures venting the unstable subterranean heat of the earth's mantle. If Vulcanus isn't challenged regularly to release this built-up energy, the entire jungle sanctuary would split wide open in a catastrophic volcanic eruption.

The tragic, epic twist of his lore involves his eternal connection to his elemental brother, Lycanthros (The Blue Buff). While Lycanthros represents the cool, rapid static electricity of the atmosphere, Vulcanus represents the dense, crushing kinetic heat of the deep earth. They are the two binary pillars of the jungle’s health.

Yet, by cosmic design, they can never leave their respective camps to meet. They are trapped in a simultaneous cycle of endless execution and resurrection by mortal hands. Vulcanus knows that the moment he is slain, his brother across the river is likely suffering the exact same fate, their souls constantly dissolving back into the leyline roots only to reform 90 seconds later to fight the exact same mortal greed all over again.

His Savage Weapon: The Molten Cleaver Glaive
To channel his immense, high-temperature kinetic force, Vulcanus brandishes a weapon of absolute elemental ruin: the Molten Cleaver Glaive. This towering polearm measures an imposing 230 cm in length, featuring a thick, perfectly balanced shaft crafted from polished, blackened volcanic timber that has been naturally petrified by intense heat. The grip is wrapped loosely in thin bands of golden leather, terminating in a massive, weighted golden hook at the base.

The business end of the glaive is where things get truly catastrophic. It sports a complex, multi-pronged crescent blade forged from a singular, massive chunk of translucent orange crystal. This crystal doesn't just cut; it vibrates violently with active, high-temperature heat currents, melting steel armor on contact before the blade even touches the physical flesh beneath. Suspended within a hollow cavity at the direct center of the crystal blades is a secondary, floating magma core. This core pulses rhythmically, drawing thermal energy directly from Vulcanus's own body to ensure the blade remains at a constant, white-hot sharpening temperature.

His Catastrophic Power: The Scorching Ruin Aura
Vulcanus does not merely utilize fire; his volcanic anatomy projects an overwhelming, suffocating environment known as the Scorching Ruin. He is permanently enveloped in a dense, rapidly spinning field of pale-yellow fire and deep-orange energy arcs that twist around his silhouette like a localized firestorm. The air within a twenty-meter radius of his boulder becomes violently warped by a thick heat haze, smelling intensely of fresh sulfur, dry ash, and raw kinetic heat.

When he prepares to swing his massive glaive, his obsidian pauldrons—the jagged volcanic stone shards anchoring his shoulders—flare with internal light. His neon-yellow, pupil-less almond eyes leak heavy trails of smoldering ash as he unleashes his fury. This aura projects an immense, paralyzing psychological pressure. The sheer ambient heat cooks the air out of his enemies' lungs, inducing absolute panic and reducing their combat efficiency as they realize they aren't just fighting a warrior—they are fighting the living wrath of an ancient, incinerated god.








Name: Lithos, The Earthen Core of the Riverlands (Litho wanderer From MLBB)
Diminutive Earth-Sprite Physiology and Childlike Geomorphic Facial Structure
This character stands as a remarkably unique, small-scale manifestation of the Land of Dawn’s riverbed magic, possessing a diminutive, compact, and highly agile physical stature that reaches a modest height of 115 cm. His body type is an extraordinary exhibition of dense, rock-solid earth-sprite anatomy fused with a vibrant, playful energy—exceptionally light on his feet yet possessing a stocky, dense physical framework composed of living river stone and hyper-condensed crystal. His facial structure is an endearing, rounded masterwork of ancient geomorphic beauty, making him look like a youthful forest spirit frozen at a childlike maturity that mirrors a human around eight to ten years old. He features a soft, smooth jawline that seamlessly curves into a small chin, a tiny, slightly button-like nose, and rounded cheekbones that emit a faint luminescence whenever he expresses joy or curiosity. His skin tone is a brilliant, smooth jade-green and rich moss-color, deeply polished like a river stone that has been smoothed over centuries by rushing currents, accented by glowing turquoise-blue fault lines that pulse gently across his temples. His eyes are large, expressive, and perfectly round pools of a brilliant, blinding neon-cyan color that completely lack human pupils or irises, constantly shining with an innocent, curious light that conveys a pure connection to the natural lifecycle of the river camp.

The Geomorphic Sprout-Crown and the Crystallized Aquamarine Tresses
His head is defined by a naturally grown, protective arrangement of geomorphic elements that visually anchor his identity as a sentient river blossom. He does not wear a manufactured helmet, metallic visor, or tailored cloth cap; instead, his brow is crowned by an integrated ring of thick, overlapping emerald-green and gold-tipped stone sepals that resemble the protective outer petals of a closed lotus flower. This living stone crown organically forms a protective shield around his skull, rising into soft, smooth peaks that frame his face. Beneath the structured perimeter of this earthen crest, his hair is a magnificent, glowing mass of pure, liquefied crystal that flows upward and backward like a slow-moving, weightless fountain. This crystalline coiffure possesses a vibrant aquamarine-blue hue at the base that transitions into a brilliant, translucent yellow-green at the tips, moving with a gentle, floating rhythm that defies regular gravity and sheds tiny, sparkling specks of pollen-like light into the surrounding air whenever he moves his head.

The Moss-Weave Vest and Crystalline Shoulder Carapaces
The upper body attire of this character is a spectacular, minimalist exhibition of natural riverbed elements designed to match his light, agile movements while providing dense geomorphic protection. He wears a form-fitting, sleeveless vest woven entirely from ancient, dense river moss and reinforced roots dyed a deep forest-green, leaving his small, solid arms fully bare to showcase the glowing turquoise veins tracing along his forearms. Attached directly to his upper shoulders and upper back are three large, overlapping crystalline carapaces that mimic the protective golden-green stone shell of a river sprite. These shell plates are polished to a mirror-like finish, curving gracefully around his shoulder blades and upper torso to act as natural pauldrons that flash with internal cyan light whenever he channels his defensive magic. His hands are small yet exceptionally firm, with fingers that end in smooth, blunt jade-like nubs, allowing him to scurry across stone surfaces or burrow into the riverbed with effortless grace.

The Lithic Tassets and the Quadrupedal Stone Greaves
Securing his natural moss vest at the midsection is a thick, twisted rope girdle woven from reinforced river reeds and golden fibers, anchoring several small, hanging smooth gray stones that rattle playfully with every step. Below the waist, his anatomy beautifully references his natural, scuttling origin, featuring a short, rounded lower torso protected by layered lithic tassets of smooth gray slate. Rather than standard human legs, his lower body splits into four highly coordinated, short, and heavy quadrupedal limbs crafted entirely from dense, weathered river boulders. These stone legs are arranged in a star-like pattern beneath his center of gravity, with each limb tapering down into solid, multi-toed stone claws that serve as natural, unbreakable sabatons. This unique lower body framework grants him unparalleled stability on slippery surfaces, allowing him to skurry sideways, climb vertical stone faces, or pivot instantly on a dime, leaving a faint trail of fresh moss, damp sand, and tiny, glowing cyan ripples across the earth wherever he roams.

The Core of Vitality Orb and the Protective Nature Aura
This character does not carry a traditional manufactured weapon like a sword or a heavy polearm; instead, he manipulates a floating, legendary elemental artifact known as the "Core of Vitality"—a brilliant, raw-cut crystal orb measuring 30 cm in diameter that hovers effortlessly just above his small hands. The exterior of this magical core is protected by three curving, golden-green jade petals that open and close in response to his emotions, while the interior houses a swirling, highly concentrated vortex of pure, life-giving aquamarine energy. The aura carried by this floating core, and Lithos himself, is a refreshing, multi-layered manifestation of "Earthen Regeneration." It continuously radiates a soft, pulsing dome of pale blue and emerald-green light fields that smell strongly of fresh rain, crushed clover, and damp river stones, lowering the temperature of the air and filling nearby allies with an immediate sense of revitalizing warmth. When he scuttles into motion, this aura leaves a vibrant, glowing trail of life-force that can accelerate the movements of nearby friendly champions and mend their wounds, acting as a small but vital beacon of hope across the battlefield.

Lore: The Playful Heart of the Sacred River
Within the grand, overarching ecosystem of the Land of Dawn, Lithos is revered as the ancient, pure soul of the riverways, acting as a small but incredibly crucial catalyst for the region's magical balance. Created by the ancient elemental lords to serve as a low-profile scout and gardener for the sacred grottos, Lithos spent millennia tending to the riverbeds, coaxing magical flora to bloom and ensuring the leyline energies flowed smoothly between the larger buff sanctuaries. Because of his pure, uncorrupted nature, he possesses no inherent malice or desire for conquest; he views the cataclysmic wars of mortals and demons with an innocent, childlike curiosity, often scuttling playfully alongside wandering heroes to grant them his coveted blessing of speed and health. However, his small size belies an absolute importance to the battlefield—if the dark forces of the Abyss ever manage to corrupt or extinguish his light, the entire river valley would immediately wither into a toxic, dried-out wasteland, forcing Lithos to use his incredible speed and reality-bending agility to stay one step ahead of those who wish to exploit his life-giving core for dark purposes.

Suggested Atmospheric Background
Lithos would look exceptionally magnificent scuttling across a smooth, wet granite stone located right at the edge of a shallow, crystal-clear river delta during a serene morning dawn. The background should feature the grand, ancient architecture of the Elemental Sanctuary rising in the distance, with massive stone arches and gnarled roots framing a soft, misty background where low-lying river fog catches the early morning sun. The lighting should be a bright, cinematic "Dew-Drop Radiance," where the soft, golden-pink rays of the rising sun filter through heavy jungle canopy leaves, catching the translucent, liquefied aquamarine textures of his hair and reflecting intensely off the polished surfaces of his jade skin. This clean, high-contrast lighting should perfectly emphasize the rich mossy textures of his vest and the brilliant, neon-cyan glow of his wide round eyes. A soft, swirling mist of glowing green particles from his nature aura should be shown pooling around his four stone feet, blending seamlessly into the ripples of the shallow riverbank, capturing his endearing yet mystical presence as the ultimate, eternal child of the earth.


