Long before the modern factions dug their defensive trenches, the primordial elemental lords realized the Land of Dawn's leylines needed a mobile, low-profile caretaker to prevent magical runoff from stagnating. They sculpted Lithos—a 115 cm tall earth-sprite composed of living jade-stone, rich moss, and a gravity-defying mane of liquefied aquamarine crystal. He is famous across the realm because he holds no malice and takes no sides; he is an innocent, childlike gardener of the grottos. Yet, his importance to the ecosystem is absolute. If a dark faction from the Abyss were to ever permanently corrupt his pure core, the entire river valley would wither into a toxic, dried-out wasteland.🍃 Why He is Famous: The Kingmaker of the Two-Minute MarkThough he appears cute, Lithos is universally famous for dictating the entire tempo of the early game. In the strategic manuals of elite assassins and mages, securing Lithos at the early-game river junction is the ultimate milestone.He carries a two-part spiritual boon: when defeated in honorable combat, his symbiotic partner—the parasitic plant known as the Walkie Grass—willingly detaches and follows the victorious champion, continuously feeding them mana and a significant boost to movement speed. Simultaneously, Lithos transforms into a persistent, unkillable Stone Roamer sentry in the riverbed. This sentry beams a permanent, radar-like vision feed directly to the team's map, exposing incoming enemy ambushes, securing safe passages to the Turtle pit, and acting as the absolute kingmaker for early-game macro rotation.  🔮 The Mythic Lore: The Cabbage and the ParasiteThe historical novels of the Cadia Riverlands reveal an incredibly deep, symbiotic biological secret about why Lithos exists in two parts. Lithos’s physical body is actually a rare, highly condensed geomorphic gemstone creature. The lush, vibrant sprout crowning his head—the Geomorphic Sprout-Crown—is actually a separate, sentient parasitic entity called the Walkie Grass.  In ancient times, the Walkie Grass actively stole Lithos’s inherent vision capabilities, blinding the little earth spirit and forcing them to scuttle together as a single unit. When a hero strikes Lithos on the battlefield, the impact doesn't destroy him; it temporarily shatters the genetic bond between the host and the parasite.Upon splitting, Lithos instantly regains his true, omniscient earthen sight, gratefully projecting a scouting ward to grant his savior map vision. Meanwhile, the energetic Walkie Grass hitches a ride on the victorious hero, happily feeding them movement-accelerating energy. It is a beautiful, tragic cycle of perpetual separation and reunion that keeps the river leylines perfectly synchronized.  🔮 His Floating Artifact: The Core of VitalityLithos does not wield a crude weapon forged of cold iron or steel. Instead, he manipulates a legendary elemental artifact known as the Core of Vitality—a brilliant, raw-cut crystal orb measuring 30 cm in diameter that hovers effortlessly just above his small, jade-nubbed hands.The Self-Defense BatteryThe Jade Sepal Carapace: The exterior of this floating magical core is shielded by three curving, golden-green jade petals. These petals organically open and close in real-time response to Lithos's innocent emotions, hardening into a defensive shield if he senses incoming hostility.The Aquamarine Vortex: The interior of the orb houses a violently swirling, highly concentrated vortex of pure, life-giving aquamarine energy. Rather than shooting destructive beams, this core acts as a kinetic battery, pulsing outward to alter the gravitational weight of things around him.🌿 His Innocent Power: Earthen RegenerationDespite his childlike facial structure and small height, Lithos commands a localized, reality-bending environmental aura known as Earthen Regeneration. This manifests as a soft, pulsing dome of pale blue and emerald-green light fields that smells strongly of fresh rain, crushed clover, and damp river stones.1. The Quadrupedal Scuttle DashWhen threatened, Lithos relies on his unique anatomy. His lower body features a star-like arrangement of four highly coordinated, short, and heavy quadrupedal limbs crafted entirely from dense river boulders. These stone legs allow him to ignore slippery terrain, climbing vertical rock faces or scurrying sideways with absolute stability. When he activates his aura, his crystallized aquamarine tresses burn upward like a slow-moving fountain, dropping sparkling light particles that grant massive movement speed boosts to nearby friendly units.2. The Leyline RefreshWhen Lithos actively channels the Core of Vitality, his nature aura expands along the ground in tiny, glowing cyan ripples. This energy field rapidly recalibrates the spiritual energy of any champion standing near him. For allies, it causes a soothing, revitalizing warmth that mends minor battle wounds and rapidly restores depleted mana reserves, allowing spellcasters to continue fighting without needing to retreat all the way back to their base sanctuary.🥬 The Twist: The Great River Hide-and-Seek ExtravaganzaWhile the grand, historic records paint Lithos as a vital, solemn guardian node of the river ecosystem, the casual journals of the wandering river crabs (Scuttlers) reveal that Lithos has the attention span of a literal toddler. Because he possesses no inherent malice and treats the catastrophic, bloody wars of the mortal factions as a giant, elaborate game of tag, he is a constant source of stress for the jungle's larger guardians.According to a hilarious entry from an Eruditio scout's notebook, a highly organized, tense standoff between the forces of the Moniyan Empire and the Shadow Abyss over the first Turtle spawn was completely derailed because Lithos unexpectedly scuttled right out of the bushes, giggling with a sound like rattling river stones.He proceeded to playfully headbutt a terrifying Abyssal demon, stole a shiny gold ring off a Moniyan commander's gauntlet using his mouth, and then scuttled sideways into the river current at supersonic speeds. Both armies were so utterly bewildered by the tiny cabbage-monster's sudden chaotic drive-by that they completely forgot their tactical formations, turning a historic, map-defining battle into an unorganized, muddy game of hide-and-seek trying to track down where the glowing blue crystal hair went.











Name: Karkinos, The Scholar of the Emerald Shallows (Exp Crab of MLBB)
Crustacean-Sage Physiology and the Intellectual Facial Structure
This character presents an extraordinary, highly distinct personification of the Land of Dawn’s coastal waterways, possessing a highly compact, agile, and asymmetric male physical stature that settles at a unique height of 152 cm. His body type is a fascinating exhibition of high-density, lean, and wiry muscle mass combined with heavy, naturally grown chitinous armor plates—broad-shouldered, low-centered, and displaying a posture that balances intellectual poise with the quick, lateral mobility of a shore-dwelling creature. His facial structure is an arresting masterwork of youthful, sharp intelligence, making him look like a brilliant wandering archivist or scribe frozen at a maturity that mirrors a human in his late teens or early twenties. He features a highly defined, angular jawline that slopes tightly toward a firm chin, a small, straight nose, and high, sharp cheekbones that give his face a keen, discerning expression. His skin tone is a warm, sun-kissed tan with smooth, pearlescent textures, accented along his temples and jaw by tiny, naturally grown patches of sandy-bronze shell fragments. His eyes are his most captivating feature: large, intensely sharp, and almond-shaped orbs of a brilliant, burning neon-cyan color that completely lack human pupils or irises, constantly shining with an ancient, calculating wisdom and leaking faint trails of shimmering turquoise light from their corners to convey an expression of absolute focus and heightened tactical perception.

The Scholar’s Silk Hood and the Glistening Aquamarine Topknot
His head is defined by an exquisite, scholarly arrangement of protective textiles and vibrant, crystalline hair that underscores his status as a traveling keeper of forbidden knowledge. He does not wear a metal war helmet or a rigid defensive visor; instead, his brow is framed by an open-faced, traditional scholar’s hood crafted from thick, sandy-beige silk fabric. This tailored hood wraps securely around the back of his skull and neck, featuring intricate, spiraling geometric glyphs embroidered in gold thread along the perimeter to shield him from the coastal winds. Beneath the structured frame of this fabric hood, his hair is a magnificent, spiky mass of thick, heavy locks that carry a rich, multi-toned coloration, shifting from a deep indigo-purple at the roots to a brilliant, glowing aquamarine-blue at the tips. This thick hair is swept upward and tightly bound at the crown of his head into a high, gravity-defying topknot style, secured firmly by a small golden ring. Several jagged strands are left free at the front to frame his face, crackling faintly with internal magical energy and constantly shedding tiny, glittering particles of stardust into the air whenever he moves his head.

The Chitinous Pauldrons and the Scroll-Bound Back Carapace
The upper body attire of this character is a spectacular, seamless marriage of lightweight wandering scholar robes and heavy, organic crustacean defenses designed to safeguard his prized possessions. He wears a high-collared, form-fitting tunic of deep royal-purple silk that is tightly wrapped across his chest, leaving his right arm fully exposed to showcase his lean musculature and a series of cyan elemental glyphs tracking down to his hand. His left shoulder is heavily fortified by an oversized, asymmetric pauldron sculpted from thick, hardened sandy-bronze chitin that extends forward like a defensive shield to mimic the massive, crushing claw of an alpha crustacean. Mounted directly to his upper back, resting atop a heavy platform of protective violet shell plates, is his most sacred burden: a massive, tightly rolled ancient parchment scroll bound securely by thick, purple silk cords. Erupting from beneath this historic scroll are several large, jagged clusters of pure, translucent aquamarine crystal spikes that flare upward like protective wing-like protrusions, pulsing with internal energy and casting a brilliant, multi-colored rim light across his shoulders.

The Reed Girdle and the Multipedal Tassel Skirt
Securing his exquisite, scholarly vestments at the midsection is an exceptionally wide, multi-layered battle-belt woven from reinforced river reeds and golden fibers, fastened at the center with a large, circular gold-iron buckle etched with ancient marine runes. Hanging from this belt is a highly unique, multi-paneled war-skirt composed of heavy, asymmetric panels of sandy-beige canvas and purple silk that mimic the segmented architecture of a shore-crab's under-shell. Beneath this protective skirt, his lower body type completely transcends normal human design, bypassing standard legs, trousers, or footwear. Instead, his lower half features a specialized, low-slung lower torso from which four highly articulated, segmented arthropod legs emerge in a wide, lateral star-pattern. These limbs are forged from the same rock-hard, sandy-bronze chitin as his left pauldron, with each leg curving sharply downward to terminate in a polished, needle-sharp point that serves as a natural sabaton. This unique multipedal framework allows him to skurry sideways with blinding speed, climb vertical wet cliffs, or pivot instantly across slippery terrain, leaving a trail of crushed sand, tiny shell fragments, and glowing cyan script ripples across the earth wherever he roams.

The Sovereign Crystal Stylus and the Shimmering Arcane Aura
This character wields a highly unusual, deceptively lethal weapon known as the "Sovereign Crystal Stylus"—a massive, one-handed staff-sized writing tool measuring an imposing 180 cm in length. The shaft is a slender, perfectly balanced column of polished, dark-purple coral wrapped tightly in thin bands of golden leather for an unbreakable grip, finishing in a weighted golden base hook. The apex of the weapon features a massive, jaggedly curved single claw forged from a pure, translucent aquamarine crystal that vibrates violently with active magical currents, housing a swirling core of concentrated experience energy at its center. The aura carried by this weapon, and Karkinos himself, is an overwhelming, multi-layered manifestation of "Absolute Archivist." It continuously radiates a soft, pulsing dome of pale blue and smoky lavender light fields that smell strongly of ancient parchment, salt water, and cold river moss, distorting the lighting around his silhouette. When he channels his power or scripts a spell in the dirt, this aura flares violently into a flashing ring of golden geometric runes, projecting a heavy psychological pressure that fills his enemies with immediate fatigue and confusion, symbolizing the crushing weight of centuries of recorded history.

Lore: The Wandering Archivist of the Experience Lane
Within the grand, cyclical ecosystem of the Land of Dawn, Karkinos is revered as the legendary, timeless scholar of the outer shores, acting as the ultimate guardian of the realm's accumulated knowledge and martial experience. Born from a sacred coastal delta where the leylines of the forest meet the infinite memory of the sea, Karkinos was blessed with a hyper-intelligent mind, choosing to spend his centuries wandering the battlegrounds to record the histories, triumphs, and tragic falls of mortal heroes. Because his small form contains a fragment of the world's primal core, his back carapace naturally grew the sacred Scroll of Ascension, an artifact that continuously absorbs the kinetic essence of battle and converts it into pure, soul-elevating experience energy. He is an independent, neutral sage who takes no side in the wars between empires and the Abyss; instead, he roams the outer lanes of the battlefield, testing the tactical brilliance of passing champions. To defeat him in a trial of combat is to unlock the ultimate secrets of his scroll, as Karkinos willingly bestows his coveted blessing of wisdom and rapid ascension to those who possess the raw potential to shape the future of the Land of Dawn.

Suggested Atmospheric Background
Karkinos would look exceptionally magnificent standing atop a mossy granite outcrop right at the shoreline of a misty, ancient river delta during a dramatic golden dawn. The background should feature the grand, sweeping architecture of a forgotten coastal ruin rising through a sea of low-lying morning fog, with gnarled mangrove roots and shallow, emerald-green water channels catching the early morning sun. The lighting should be a bright, highly cinematic "Coastal Radiance," where the soft, pink-and-gold rays of the rising sun strike the landscape from a low angle, casting long shadows and creating a majestic rim light that catches the translucent, liquefied aquamarine textures of his topknot and reflects intensely off the polished surfaces of his sandy-bronze armor plates. This high-contrast lighting should perfectly emphasize the rich, fibrous textures of his silk robes and the unblinking, neon-cyan brilliance of his eyes. A soft, swirling mist of glowing purple particles and tiny floating glyphs from his archivist aura should be shown pooling around his four chitinous feet, blending beautifully into the ripples of the shallow riverbank, capturing his unique, statuesque presence as a mystical guardian watching over the cradle of history.

