While historical tapestries paint Plutus as a majestic, neutral financial deity guarding the cradle of commerce, the personal logs of marksmen reveal that the crab-sage is an incredibly petty, highly bureaucratic loan shark. He does not simply hand over his gold out of the goodness of his heart; he values perfect financial ledger accuracy above human life.

According to a hilarious field report from a rogue Eruditio mechanic, a Bruno player once tried to trick Plutus by kicking a counterfeit gold coin into his pit to see if it would bait the crab out early. Plutus did not just ignore the coin; he allegedly used his Sovereign Crystal Stylus to look up the marksman’s global combat history, calculated the exact amount of map damage Bruno had caused over his career, and then targeted him with an aura that temporarily reduced his attack speed by 50% for "unauthorized tax evasion."

If your posture isn't up to his aristocratic standards, or if you attempt to claim his bounty without a clean financial record, Plutus will happily scuttle sideways at mach speeds, clicking his giant bronze claw mockingly while making a sound like a broken cash register, leaving you broke and completely exposed to an enemy ambush.









Name: Genbu, The Unyielding Bulwark of the Sunken Sanctum (Turtle of MLBB)
Reptilian-Deity Physiology and the Ancient Sovereign Facial Structure
This character stands as a monumental, deeply revered personification of the Land of Dawn’s ancient river systems, presenting a colossal, heavily armored, and immensely powerful male physical stature that reaches a towering height of 215 cm. His body type is an extraordinary exhibition of gargantuan, high-density muscular power and absolute defensive mass—characterized by an exceptionally broad chest, massive shoulders, and a thick, indestructible physical framework that perfectly mirrors a legendary dragon-turtle kin or an ancient primeval deity. His facial structure is a majestic, chiseled masterwork of stoic authority, making him look like an ancient, timeless warrior-king frozen at a mature age that mirrors a human in his late thirties or early forties. He features a wide, immensely powerful square jawline that feels as solid as a continental shelf, a prominent noble nose, and deep, pronounced cheekbones that give his face an unmoving, stone-like countenance. His skin tone is an otherworldly, pale jade-white across his neck, jaw, and chest, transitioning seamlessly into a thick, heavily textured jade-green dermis across his limbs, which is deeply detailed with natural reptilian scale formations that catch the light like polished gemstone matrixes. His eyes are wide, intensely sharp, and almond-shaped orbs of a brilliant, glowing neon-cyan color that completely lack human pupils or irises, constantly pulsing with a serene, ancient wisdom and leaking faint trails of shimmering turquoise vapor from their corners to convey an expression of absolute, eternal focus and unbreakable willpower.

The Dragon-Horn Coronet and the Churned Aquamarine Mane
His head is defined by a magnificent, naturally grown skeletal structure and a vibrant, flowing mane of hair that underscores his absolute sovereign status over the riverbed domains. He does not wear a standard manufactured war helmet, iron visor, or cloth cowl; instead, a massive, multi-tiered sovereign crown forged from a polished sea-gold alloy curves gracefully from his brow line, sweeping backward into sharp, stylized ridges that blend seamlessly with a pair of elegant, sweeping dragon horns. These golden-bronze horns erupt directly from the sides of his temples, curving smoothly backward and tapering into sharp, jagged points that accentuate the royal architecture of his skull. Beneath the structured frame of this divine crest, his hair is a voluminous, flowing mass of living, liquefied sapphire-blue current that completely ignores the laws of gravity. This watery mane moves as if permanently submerged in a deep, heavy current, floating in a slow-motion weightless dance around his shoulders and cascading down his upper back like a localized, churning waterfall that constantly sheds tiny, glowing droplets of moisture into the air.

The Jade Sunburst Carapace and Upper Body Heavy Plating
The upper body attire of this character is an extraordinary, form-fitting exhibition of heavy, ornamental plate armor fused completely with his massive, half-human, half-aquatic anatomy. He wears a highly stylized, deep chest piece forged from an ancient, high-grade gold-bronze alloy that has been sculpted to accentuate his massive chest while allowing his scaled form to flow seamlessly through the gaps. The shoulders are protected by two oversized, asymmetric sunburst pauldrons that sweep upward like defensive shields, with the left shoulder expanding into a massive, multi-tiered geometric crescent structure that frames the back of his head like a sacred halo. His massive arms are heavily scaled and partially bare to showcase his immense strength, but his wrists and forearms are fully encased in heavy, articulated golden vambraces etched with primal waves. His hands are exceptionally large and powerful, featuring thick fingers that terminate in blunt, jade-like talons capable of crushing solid stone or channeling massive kinetic forces to lock weapons with the most imposing behemoths of the battlefield.

The Segmented Arch-Girdle and the Great Dragon-Shell Train
Securing his magnificent upper armor plates at the midsection is an exceptionally wide, heavy double-tiered arch-girdle made of polished sea-gold, tightly cinching his waist to distribute the immense weight of his upper torso defenses. At the direct center of this belt sits an oversized, geometric circular buckle etched with the primal crest of the Sunken Sanctum, anchoring two long, segmented golden plates that drape down diagonally to shield his outer thighs. Mounted directly to his upper back, acting as a colossal defensive shield, is his most defining feature: a magnificent, domed shell mantle crafted from pure, translucent teal-blue crystal and reinforced by interlocking golden-bronze skeletal ridges. This massive dragon-carapace flares outward and downward behind him like a royal train, its smooth panels pulsing with an internal neon-cyan bioluminescence. Below the waist, he wears tattered, dark indigo combat trousers that are heavily bound along the shins by thick canvas cords, leading down into massive, clawed metal sabatons that mimic the heavy, multi-toed paws of a mythical beast, allowing him to dig into the earth and anchor his weight with absolute stability.

The Bulwark Scepter of Radiance and the Crushing Aquatic Aura
This character wields a catastrophic, beautifully terrifying legendary polearm weapon known as the "Bulwark Scepter of Radiance"—a towering, two-handed staff of absolute aquatic dominion measuring an imposing 240 cm in length. The shaft is a solid, unyielding column of reinforced gold-iron alloy wrapped in thin spirals of silver wire for an unbreakable grip, finishing in a weighted, blunt golden pommel. The massive head of the scepter features three elongated, razor-sharp prongs forged from a pure, translucent cyan crystal that vibrates violently with internal magical current, creating a weapon that functions simultaneously as a sovereign trident and a channeling staff. The aura carried by this weapon, and Genbu himself, is an overwhelming, suffocating manifestation of "Absolute Bulwark." It manifests as a dense, rolling mist of teal and gold energy fields that constantly swirl around his silhouette like a protective dome, smelling faintly of clean rain, fresh ozone, and cold river moss. When he slams the base of his trident into the earth, this aura expands into sharp, geometric waves of kinetic force that crackle violently along the ground, signaling a defensive and offensive power so absolute that it can knock back an entire army without shifting a single inch of his stance.

Lore: The Ancient Vanguard of the Sacred Riverlands
Within the deep, primordial lore of the Land of Dawn, Genbu is revered as the legendary, first-born guardian of the world's natural elements, created by the ancient forces to serve as the ultimate trial of endurance for mortal heroes. Long before the modern empires built their stone capitals, Genbu governed the sacred riverbeds and subterranean grottos, acting as an impartial force of nature that maintained the delicate equilibrium between the living earth and the chaotic entities of the void. When the modern conflicts began to tear the realm apart, Genbu chose to anchor his essence within the sacred waters, manifesting as a colossal, armored sentinel of stone and water to guard the ultimate fonts of economic and defensive power. He is an elemental god who does not answer to the political decrees of kings, generals, or high-priests; instead, he slumbers within his ancient sanctuary, waiting for a champion possessing the absolute purity of spirit and strength of arm required to best him in combat. To defeat him is to earn the supreme blessing of the earth itself, as Genbu willingly lends his unstoppable, shielding fury and a massive bounty of team-wide armor to those he deems worthy of ending the world's turmoils and restoring peace to the land.

Suggested Atmospheric Background
Genbu would look exceptionally magnificent standing at the absolute center of a hidden, primordial river shrine located within a deep, mist-shrouded jungle canyon at midnight. The background should feature towering, ancient grey granite cliffs carved with massive, moss-covered geometric ruins, with clean waterfalls cascading down the rock faces into a sprawling, perfectly still turquoise pool. The lighting should be a majestic, high-contrast "Bioluminescent Midnight," where the cool, dark indigo of the night sky is sharply broken by the vibrant, neon-cyan light radiating directly from his own fluid mane and the crystal prongs of his scepter, casting dancing reflections across the wet stone walls. This dramatic, atmospheric lighting should perfectly catch the polished, reflective surfaces of his heavy gold armor plates, the translucent depths of his teal dragon-shell mantle, and the unblinking brilliance of his turquoise eyes. Thick wisps of cooling river fog and glowing energy particles from his bulwark aura should be shown pooling around his heavy sabatons, blending seamlessly into the ripples of the shallow riverbank, capturing his immense, statuesque presence as an eternal god watching over the cradle of life.

An epic breakdown of one of the Land of Dawn's most hard-carrying neutral deities is detailed below. We are taking the gameplay mechanics you know and smashing them straight into the high-fantasy novel lore, giving Genbu the absolute legendary status he deserves—with a few fun twists.

Genbu, The Unyielding Bulwark of the Sunken Sanctum
The Epic Lore: The Ancient Vanguard of the Sacred Riverlands
In the dusty, ink-stained pages of Cadia’s oldest historical chronicles, Genbu isn't just a "neutral objective" that jungle mains aggressively ping at the two-minute mark. He is a literal primeval deity. Long before the Moniyan Empire laid its first foundation stones or the Scarlet Shadow ninjas began their eternal family feuds, Genbu was designated by the ancient world-forging powers to regulate the chaotic, roaring river systems of the Land of Dawn.

He spent millennia slumbering in the crystal-veined grottos beneath the riverbeds, completely unbothered by the shifting political boundaries of mortals.

Why is He Famous?
To the common folk of the Cadia Riverlands, Genbu is famous as the literal bedrock of life. To the high-tier heroes who cross blades in the arena, he is known as The Great Equalizer. Genbu does not side with light, darkness, or whatever questionable experiment the Eruditio scientists are cooking up this week. He is an absolute force of cosmic equilibrium.

The Immortal Myth: Lore novels dictate that Genbu's spiritual weight is so massive that his physical manifestation directly mirrors the economic and defensive health of the surrounding ecosystem. When he is roused, he offers an ultimate trial of martial endurance.

In-universe, he doesn't actually "die" when a hyper-carry hero lands a Retribution spell on him. Instead, he judges their raw power, nods in stoic approval, and willingly shatters his own aura to coat the victorious team in a legendary, sweeping matrix of defensive crystal energy. Basically, he gives your team a massive armor boost because he respects your hustle.

The Weapon: The Bulwark Scepter of Radiance
Forget standard steel swords or magically enchanted daggers. Genbu walks into battle wielding a catastrophic, beautifully terrifying legendary polearm known as the Bulwark Scepter of Radiance.

Measuring an imposing 240 cm in length, this weapon is a masterwork of divine craftsmanship. The main shaft is forged from an unyielding gold-iron alloy wrapped in delicate, razor-thin spirals of conductive silver wire to ensure his grip never slips, even when drenched in the blood of invading void demons. The staff terminates in an incredibly heavy, blunt golden pommel designed to break the landmasses themselves.

