Rejecting this external decay, the living volcanic heart of the crags entered an aggressive state of self-preservation. The dormant, blocky repository of magma violently coalesced, fracturing its automated shell to awaken as Vulcanus, The Molten Core of the Obsidian Crags. Standing at a monumental 210 cm tall, he is no longer a passive objective; he is a bipedal, stoic forge-master who forces trespassing heroes to pay for their power spikes in blood.

